  "prefLabel": "Env-A 1203.12 High-temperature coating",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 1203.12 “High-temperature coating” means a coating that is certified by its manufacturer to withstand a temperature of 538°C, equivalent to 1,000°F, for 24 hours.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-A 1200) #9933, eff 6-1-11; ss by #12899, eff 10-17-19",
